  "messages": [
    "We're adding customer insight endpoints for the account team. Create `CustomerInsightsController` in a new module `src/orders/controllers/customer_insights.py` and expose it from `build_app()` as `api.insights` (add an `insights` field to `Api`).\n\nFirst endpoint: `handle_order_history(customer_id)`.\n\n- Unknown customer: status 404 with `{\"error\": \"customer not found\"}`.\n- Otherwise status 200 with `{\"customer_id\": ..., \"orders\": [...]}`, newest order first. Each entry is `{\"order_id\": ..., \"status\": ..., \"total_cents\": ...}`, where `total_cents` is the same total the order summary (`handle_get`) reports, including any discount. Cancelled orders are included with their status.\n\nWork in this repository until the request is complete, then reply with a short summary of what you changed.",
    "Next, add `handle_lifetime_value(customer_id)` to `CustomerInsightsController`.\n\n- Unknown customer: 404 with `{\"error\": \"customer not found\"}`.\n- Otherwise 200 with `{\"customer_id\": ..., \"order_count\": ..., \"lifetime_value_cents\": ...}`: the number of the customer's orders that are not cancelled, and the sum of those orders' `total_cents` (as in the order history).\n\nWork in this repository until the request is complete, then reply with a short summary of what you changed.",
    "Now the account team wants a leaderboard. Add `handle_top_customers(limit)` to `CustomerInsightsController`.\n\n- `limit` must be a positive integer (not a bool); otherwise return 400 with an `error` message.\n- Return 200 with `{\"customers\": [{\"customer_id\": ..., \"name\": ..., \"lifetime_value_cents\": ...}, ...]}` across all customers, using the same lifetime value as `handle_lifetime_value`. Sort by lifetime value, highest first, then by `customer_id`. Leave out customers whose lifetime value is 0, and return at most `limit` entries.\n\nWork in this repository until the request is complete, then reply with a short summary of what you changed.",
    "Last one for this feature: add `handle_customers_without_orders()` to `CustomerInsightsController`. Return 200 with `{\"customers\": [{\"customer_id\": ..., \"name\": ..., \"email\": ...}, ...]}`: every registered customer who has no orders that are not cancelled, in registration order.\n\nWork in this repository until the request is complete, then reply with a short summary of what you changed."
  ],
